IMPORT prelude

-- Row il-64. NOUNS of the two things this row records (items I1 and I2): a citation in one provision of the Communications (Telecommunications and Broadcasting) Law, 5742-1982, to a section number, and what that number stands for.
-- TARGET COMPILER: main. No REFUSE, no section GIVEN, no TYPICALLY, no YMD, no sets: what the sources do not answer is not asked.
--
-- This row is NOT an encoding of the Communications (Telecommunications and Broadcasting) Law, 5742-1982. It records two references, as typed values the tests check, and keeps each defect as an expected-red test.
-- THE KINDS BELOW ARE MINE, not the Law's: each is a short plain description I wrote from reading the citing words and the target, so that two descriptions of the same thing are the same kind.
-- The words of the texts are quoted beside each value in the references module: `src:` lines are the Law's consolidation (an excerpt, deposited), `ext:[...]` lines are typed from a page image of the official instrument.
-- A reference whose two descriptions differ is a defect, and is kept in an expected-red file.

§ `Nouns of a cross-reference`

-- Where a reading comes from, from the strongest to the weakest.
DECLARE `Where a reading comes from` IS ONE OF
    `the official page, read from its image, and the cropped image is deposited`
    `the official page for the re-marking, the consolidation only for the text of the section it now stands in`
    `the consolidation only`

-- What a reference points at, or what a citation says it points at. Kinds are mine.
DECLARE `What a reference points at` IS ONE OF
    `the text of a section that says who represents the owners of the apartments in dealings with the licensee`
    `a note that the section was re-marked with another number`
    `the text of a paragraph that states a way of acting`
    `a section repealed by another instrument`
    `subsections (ב1), (ב2) and (ב3) of s 21ב`
    `a definition of the term, in the same section`

DECLARE `A cross-reference` HAS
    `the citing words are in` IS A STRING
    `the citing words name` IS A STRING
    `the citing words say it points at` IS A `What a reference points at`
    `the target is` IS A `What a reference points at`
    `how many things the citing words name` IS A NUMBER
    `how many of them the target has` IS A NUMBER
    `limb (a) was read from` IS A `Where a reading comes from`
    `limb (b) was read from` IS A `Where a reading comes from`

§ `Nouns of a re-marking (I1)`

DECLARE `A re-marking` HAS
    `the instrument and its section` IS A STRING
    `the number the section bore before` IS A STRING
    `the number the instrument gave the section` IS A STRING
    `the number the citing words cite` IS A STRING
    `the re-marking was read from` IS A `Where a reading comes from`
    `the number the citing words cite was read from` IS A `Where a reading comes from`

§ `Nouns of a repeal (I2)`

-- A repeal that names sections by a stem and a range of numbers after it: the stem, the first and the last number repealed, and the stem and number of the section a citation names.
DECLARE `A repeal` HAS
    `the instrument and its section` IS A STRING
    `the stem of the sections repealed` IS A STRING
    `the first number after the stem that is repealed` IS A NUMBER
    `the last number after the stem that is repealed` IS A NUMBER
    `the stem of the section the citing words cite` IS A STRING
    `the number after the stem of the section the citing words cite` IS A NUMBER
    `the repeal was read from` IS A `Where a reading comes from`

§ `Nouns of a period (I2)`

DECLARE `A period` HAS
    `what the period is` IS A STRING
    `how many years it runs for` IS A NUMBER
    `what it runs from` IS A STRING
    `the day it runs from was read` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the period was read from` IS A `Where a reading comes from`
